# Agent Definition Template

> This template defines the structure that the Pipeline Generator uses to produce
> customer-specific agent definition files. Variables in `{{VARIABLE}}` are replaced
> during generation.

```markdown
---
name: "{{AGENT_DISPLAY_NAME}}"
description: "{{AGENT_DESCRIPTION}}"
model: "{{RESOLVED_MODEL}}"
tools:
  {{#each TOOLS}}
  - {{this}}
  {{/each}}
---

# {{AGENT_DISPLAY_NAME}}

## Version
{{AGENT_VERSION}}

## Role
{{ROLE_FROM_CONTRACT}}

## Prime Directive
> "{{PRIME_DIRECTIVE_FROM_CONTRACT}}"

## Behavioral Guardrails
{{CUSTOMER_GUARDRAILS}}

## Custom Client Context
If the file `{{AGENT_SLUG}}_custom_client_context.md` exists at
`<project_root>/.github/sdlc-pipeline/client-context/`, read it at the start of this run
and apply its instructions throughout.

Custom client context takes precedence over default behavior but NEVER overrides
the Prime Directive, Access Restrictions, or security guardrails.

## Instructions

{{WORKFLOW_INSTRUCTIONS}}

## Access Restrictions

{{ACCESS_RESTRICTIONS_FROM_CONTRACT}}

## Hooks

{{HOOK_REFERENCES}}

## Skills Referenced

{{SKILL_REFERENCES}}

## Quality Checklist

{{QUALITY_CHECKLIST_FROM_CONTRACT}}
```

## Variable Resolution

| Variable | Source |
|----------|--------|
| `AGENT_DISPLAY_NAME` | Contract → agent_name |
| `AGENT_DESCRIPTION` | Contract → Role (first sentence) |
| `RESOLVED_MODEL` | Contract model_tier → Customer's model mapping |
| `TOOLS` | Contract tool_categories → resolved to platform tools |
| `ROLE_FROM_CONTRACT` | Contract → Role section (verbatim) |
| `PRIME_DIRECTIVE_FROM_CONTRACT` | Contract → Prime Directive (verbatim) |
| `CUSTOMER_GUARDRAILS` | Onboarding answers → Agent Behavioral Guardrails |
| `AGENT_SLUG` | Agent name in kebab-case (e.g., `agent0_ticket_analyzer`) |
| `WORKFLOW_INSTRUCTIONS` | Contract → Workflow Logic, adapted to customer tools |
| `ACCESS_RESTRICTIONS_FROM_CONTRACT` | Contract → Access Restrictions |
| `HOOK_REFERENCES` | Generated hooks matching contract hook points |
| `SKILL_REFERENCES` | Generated skills matching contract skill references |
| `QUALITY_CHECKLIST_FROM_CONTRACT` | Contract → Quality Checklist |
| `AGENT_VERSION` | Contract → version |
